## 1. Architecture

```
                         kubectl / workers / kubelets
                                     |
                                     v
                    +-------------------------------+
                    |   k8s-api.corp.example.com     |
                    |   Virtual IP 192.168.1.100     |
                    |   keepalived (VRRP) + HAProxy  |
                    |   listens on :8443             |
                    +---------------+---------------+
                                    |
              +---------------------+---------------------+
              |                     |                     |
              v                     v                     v
     +----------------+   +----------------+   +----------------+
     |    master1     |   |    master2     |   |    master3     |
     |  192.168.1.11  |   |  192.168.1.12  |   |  192.168.1.13  |
     |  kube-apiserver|   |  kube-apiserver|   |  kube-apiserver|
     |  etcd member   |   |  etcd member   |   |  etcd member   |
     |  scheduler     |   |  scheduler     |   |  scheduler     |
     |  ctrl-manager  |   |  ctrl-manager  |   |  ctrl-manager  |
     |  haproxy       |   |  haproxy       |   |  haproxy       |
     |  keepalived    |   |  keepalived    |   |  keepalived    |
     +----------------+   +----------------+   +----------------+
              \                     |                     /
               \                    |                    /
                +-------- etcd cluster (quorum 2 of 3) --+
                                    |
              +---------------------+---------------------+
              v                                           v
     +----------------+                         +----------------+
     |    worker1     |                         |    worker2     |
     |  192.168.1.21  |                         |  192.168.1.22  |
     |  kubelet       |                         |  kubelet       |
     |  containerd    |                         |  containerd    |
     |  calico-node   |                         |  calico-node   |
     +----------------+                         +----------------+
```

**Why three masters?** Cluster state lives in `etcd`, which needs a majority (quorum) of members to agree before writing. With 3 members, one can fail and 2 of 3 still form a majority. With 2 members, losing one leaves 1 of 2, which is not a majority, so the cluster freezes. Always use an odd number: 3 or 5.

**Why a load balancer?** Every worker, every kubelet and your `kubectl` need one stable address for "the API server". If that address were master1's IP, master1 dying would blind the whole cluster even though masters 2 and 3 are healthy. keepalived floats a virtual IP (VIP) to a surviving master; HAProxy on that master spreads requests across all three API servers.

**Why Calico?** Kubernetes does not ship with pod networking. Calico provides it and also enforces `NetworkPolicy` (firewall rules between pods), which simpler plugins like Flannel do not.

