## 10. Step 6 — Join the workers

> **Run on:** worker1, worker2 (and any future workers)

Use the **worker join command** saved in Step 3.2 (the one without `--control-plane` and `--certificate-key`):

```bash
sudo kubeadm join k8s-api.corp.example.com:8443 --token <token> \
  --discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:<hash>
```

Do **not** configure kubectl on workers; administration is done from masters or your workstation.

**Why:** Without the control-plane flags, kubeadm only configures the kubelet and kube-proxy and registers the node. Calico starts a `calico-node` pod on it automatically. Workers do not run etcd or the API server; they only run your application pods.

