## 12. Step 8 — Access from your workstation

> **Run on:** your laptop or admin workstation

Your workstation already uses the organisation DNS, so `k8s-api.corp.example.com` resolves.

```bash
# install kubectl (Linux/macOS example; Windows: use winget or choco)
curl -LO "https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl"
sudo install -o root -g root -m 0755 kubectl /usr/local/bin/kubectl

# copy the admin kubeconfig from any master
mkdir -p ~/.kube
scp <user>@master1.corp.example.com:/etc/kubernetes/admin.conf ~/.kube/config
chmod 600 ~/.kube/config
kubectl get nodes
```

**Why:** `admin.conf` already points at `k8s-api.corp.example.com:8443`, so no edits are needed. Treat this file as a root password; it has full cluster-admin rights. For other team members create individual users with RBAC instead of sharing it.

