## 13. Troubleshooting

> **Run on:** as indicated

### Join token expired (24 h) — any master

```bash
kubeadm token create --print-join-command
```

Prints a fresh **worker** join command.

### Certificate key expired (2 h) — any master

```bash
sudo kubeadm init phase upload-certs --upload-certs
```

Prints a new key. Build the control-plane join command as:
`<worker join command from above> --control-plane --certificate-key <new key>`

### Node stuck `NotReady` — on that node

```bash
sudo journalctl -u kubelet -f
```

Common causes: swap came back on (`swapon --show` should print nothing), containerd not using `SystemdCgroup = true`, Calico pod not running on that node (`kubectl -n calico-system get pods -o wide`).

### Pods on different nodes cannot talk — any master

```bash
kubectl -n calico-system logs -l k8s-app=calico-node --tail=50
```

Usually ports 179/tcp or 4789/udp blocked between nodes, or `custom-resources.yaml` CIDR not matching `--pod-network-cidr`.

### VIP appears on two masters at once — masters

VRRP (IP protocol 112) is being blocked between the masters by a firewall or by the hypervisor's port security. Allow it, or on VMware/Proxmox enable promiscuous mode / disable MAC filtering on the vSwitch.

### Wipe a node and redo its join — on that node

```bash
sudo kubeadm reset -f
sudo rm -rf /etc/cni/net.d $HOME/.kube
sudo iptables -F && sudo iptables -t nat -F && sudo iptables -X
sudo systemctl restart containerd
```

Then run the join command again. `reset` leaves Calico's CNI config in `/etc/cni/net.d`; removing it prevents the node from rejoining with stale network settings.

### Removing a master permanently — any surviving master

```bash
kubectl drain master3.corp.example.com --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data
kubectl delete node master3.corp.example.com
# then on master3 itself: sudo kubeadm reset -f   (this also removes its etcd member)
```

